# The Turing Test in Action

In Lesson 1, you'll walk the whole class through a slide-based version of the guessing game below.

Afterward, students debate their own stance on the Turing Test with an AI chatbot.

**Try the simulator below yourself first**: *can you always tell which response was written by AI?*

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.5;">
    <strong>&#128214; Turing test:</strong> a test in which a machine is considered intelligent if you can't tell it apart from a human in conversation.
  </div>
</div>

<hr>

<div style="width:100%; border-radius:10px; overflow:hidden; margin:20px 0;">
  <iframe
    src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/AIFY2/unit-1/turing-test-simulator.html"
    width="100%"
    height="920"
    frameborder="0"
    scrolling="no"
    title="Sort AI examples into Rule-Based Logic or Learns from Data"
    style="display:block; border-radius:10px;">
  </iframe>
</div>

</div>


